        "event": "Fire Weather Watch",
        "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
        "senderName": "NWS Boise ID",
        "headline": "Fire Weather Watch issued October 7 at 8:06PM MDT until October 9 at 6:00PM MDT by NWS Boise ID",
        "description": "...FIRE WEATHER WATCH FOR DRY/WINDY WEATHER FRIDAY AFTERNOON...\n\n.Dry and increasingly windy weather will develop Friday afternoon\nin the Owyhee Mountains and Southern Highlands in Idaho ahead of\na cold front expected to pass through on Saturday. Concern is\ngreatest in the southern half of those zones.\n\n* AFFECTED AREA...In Idaho, Fire Weather Zones 423 Owyhee\nMountains and 426 Southern Highlands.\n\n* TIMING...Friday afternoon.\n\n* WINDS...West 15 to 20 mph with gusts up to 35 mph.\n\n* RELATIVE HUMIDITY...11 to 19 percent.\n\n* TEMPERATURES...79 to 85 degrees.\n\n* IMPACTS...Any fire that develops will catch and spread\nquickly. Outdoor burning is not recommended.",
        "instruction": "A Fire Weather Watch means that critical fire weather conditions\nare possible. Listen for later forecasts and possible Red Flag\nWarnings.",
        "response": "Prepare",
        "note": null,
